diff --git a/docs/notes/P06/bang-quick.md b/docs/notes/P06/bang-quick.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..420c27c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/notes/P06/bang-quick.md
@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@
+# Task: Bang shell and quick commands (P06-11) Phase: 06 Owner: P06 slice C builder
+
+Read (reference @ `ab3fe9dffb0a89d534cb795e2a2940e5f6542056`): `hermes_cli/bang_shell.py`
+(whole), `cli.py` (quick-command runner). Research `04-cli-config.md` §3.7.2 (quick commands),
+§3.8; traps R04.27, R04.28. Closed before writing.
+Evidence: none.
+
+What it does (own words): `!cmd` at the prompt runs a shell command on the machine the CLI runs on
+without spending a model turn. It is not a way around the safety rules: the command goes through
+the same approval pipeline the agent's terminal tool uses, as a local, non-isolated command, so the
+floors (hardline, deny globs) block and a dangerous command asks the person. If the approval module
+cannot be loaded, the command is refused (fail closed — intended difference D-16.77 from the
+reference, which allows). The child environment comes only from `safety.child_env` (provider keys
+removed); if that fails nothing starts. Output (stdout and stderr merged) streams line by line.
+Quick commands are user-defined `/name` entries in `quick_commands`: `exec` runs a shell snippet with
+the same sanitised environment, a 30 s limit and redacted output; `alias` re-dispatches
+`/<target> <args>`.
+
+Inputs → outputs:
+- `is_bang(text)`: only a leading `!` after trimming counts (`fix it!` is a prompt).
+  `parse_bang(text)`: `!  ls` → `ls`; `!!` → `!`; bare `!` → "" (usage line printed).
+- `run_bang(text, ctx) -> int`: refused (non-interactive or gateway/cron marker) → 126 with a
+  line; guard unavailable → 126; blocked by the guard → 126 with the reason; env failure → 127;
+  launch failure → 127; timeout (120 s, clock-driven) → kill tree, 124; Ctrl+C or cancel → kill,
+  130 (the session survives); otherwise the exit code (non-zero shown after the output). Runs on
+  the host in the session cwd, else `terminal.cwd` from config, else the process cwd. Nothing is
+  written to the transcript.
+- `run_quick(name, spec, args, ctx) -> SlashResult`: exec → redacted output or "no output",
+  "timed out after 30s", error line; alias → `dispatch("/target args", redispatch)`; bad entry →
+  one line.
+
+Files: `src/indus/cli/bang.py`, `src/indus/cli/quick_commands.py`, `tests/unit/cli/test_bang.py`,
+`tests/unit/cli/test_quick_commands.py`.
+
+Edge cases / failure modes:
+- `!rm -rf /` → blocked by the hardline floor before anything starts.
+- `!env` → no provider key in the child (child_env blocks managed names).
+- A process that ignores its output and sleeps → the clock deadline kills the whole process group.
+- A missing or non-directory cwd → falls back to the next candidate.
+- The approval ask (a dangerous but not hardline command) goes through `ctx.ask_approval`; no
+  callback → treated as not answered (blocked, not a refusal).
+- Quick `exec` with an empty command, unknown type, alias without a target → one line each.
+- Quick alias loops (`a` → `b` → `a`) stop after a small depth with a message.
+
+Our design differences / decisions:
+- Fail closed when the guard cannot load (D-16.77, R04.27); refusal codes 126 (not run) are ours.
+- Timeout runs on the injected clock (poll loop), so tests use a fake clock with a real process.
+- Quick commands also run on the clock-driven runner (30 s), output captured then redacted with
+  `redact_output(force=True)`.
+
+Tests we will write:
+- `!rm -rf /` blocked by the floor; `fix it!` is a prompt; `!!`; bare `!`; `!env` has no provider
+  key; timeout 124 with a fake clock and a real `sleep`; Ctrl+C 130; launch failure 127; guard
+  missing refuses; dangerous command asks and deny blocks; nothing reaches the port; quick exec
+  output redacted; quick alias re-dispatch; quick timeout; env has no provider key.
+
+## Decisions for the lead
+- Exit code 126 for "not run" (refused, blocked, guard missing) — the reference returns nothing
+  there; 126 is the shell's "cannot execute" code. Easy to change.
+- Gateway/cron markers read from the scope env: `INDUS_GATEWAY_SESSION`, `INDUS_CRON_SESSION`,
+  `INDUS_SESSION_PLATFORM` (names to confirm when P14/P15 land).
+
+Compare checklist (filled after the rewrite; reopened `hermes_cli/bang_shell.py`, `cli.py`):
+- [x] leading `!` only, `!!`, bare `!` usage (test: `test_bang.py::test_parse_rules`)
+- [x] host only, session cwd then config cwd then process cwd (test: `::test_cwd_order`)
+- [x] guard missing fails closed (test: `::test_guard_missing_refuses`) — intended difference D-16.77
+- [x] sanitised env, launch fails if the sanitiser fails (test: `::test_env_failure_refuses`)
+- [x] 124 / 130 / 127 (tests: `::test_timeout_kills_with_124`, `::test_ctrl_c_kills_with_130`,
+  `::test_launch_failure_127`)
+- [x] quick exec redacted and scrubbed (tests: `test_quick_commands.py::test_exec_output_redacted`,
+  `::test_exec_env_has_no_provider_key`)
+- Deliberate differences: fail closed; clock-driven timeout; 126 for "not run"; quick `exec` shows
+  stdout and stderr merged (the reference shows stdout, else stderr); quick aliases stop after a few
+  hops; the whole process group is killed on timeout or Ctrl+C.
+- Not taken: Windows hidden-console flags (the runner uses `start_new_session` on POSIX only).
+
+## Status
+
+Done (2026-10-18).
diff --git a/docs/notes/P06/control-cmds.md b/docs/notes/P06/control-cmds.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..13ade9e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/notes/P06/control-cmds.md
@@ -0,0 +1,83 @@
+# Task: Control and info commands (P06-10) Phase: 06 Owner: P06 slice C builder
+
+Read (reference @ `ab3fe9dffb0a89d534cb795e2a2940e5f6542056`):
+`hermes_cli/cli_commands_mixin.py` (approvals, reasoning, toggles, scope flags),
+`hermes_cli/approval_mode.py` (whole), `hermes_cli/cli_model_switch_mixin.py` (skim: global
+switch, base URL handling). Research `04-cli-config.md` §3.17.2, §3.17.3, §3.21; trap R04.9.
+Closed before writing.
+Evidence: none.
+
+What it does (own words): the commands that change how the current session behaves or report on
+it. `/model` switches among providers that are already configured, through the session's
+`RouteBinding` (all or nothing), and with `--global` also saves the choice; leaving a custom
+endpoint clears its stale base URL and wire mode so the new key never goes to the old host (R04.9).
+`/reasoning` sets the effort on the ladder or shows/hides reasoning text. `/yolo` toggles
+auto-approve for this session and stores it on the session row so a resume keeps it. `/approvals`
+shows or saves the profile's approval mode through the config writer and reads it back. `/tools`
+lists tools or changes the session's toolsets (a new session, because the prompt depends on the
+tools). The info commands print what the session is, what it costs (n/a until P08) and what it can
+do. `/stop`, `/steer`, `/queue`, `/compress` and `/quit` control the running work.
+
+Inputs → outputs:
+- `/model` → current route; `/model NAME`, `/model PROVIDER:NAME`, `--provider P`, `--global`.
+  Busy → rejected. Failure (unknown provider, no key, refused window, dependent failed) → error
+  line; the binding stays on the old route.
+- `/reasoning` → level + display; `LEVEL` on `none…ultra` (session; `--global` also
+  `agent.reasoning_effort`); `show`/`hide` (REPL state).
+- `/yolo` → toggle; `ApprovalState.set_auto_approve(..., persist=set_yolo)`; pending write when the
+  row does not exist yet.
+- `/approvals [manual|smart|off]` → show; set through `writer.save`, then re-read with the loader;
+  managed or unreadable config → the error text, never an exception out of the REPL.
+- `/tools list|enable|disable NAME…` → list, or a new session with the changed toolset selection.
+- `/config` (redacted effective config), `/status`, `/context`, `/usage`, `/whoami`, `/help [filter]`,
+  `/version`, `/stop` (kill this session's background jobs + interrupt), `/steer TEXT`,
+  `/queue TEXT|list|clear|rm N`, `/compress` ("arrives with P08"), `/quit` (alias `/exit`).
+
+Files: `src/indus/cli/slash/control_cmds.py`, `tests/unit/cli/slash/test_control_cmds.py`.
+
+Edge cases / failure modes:
+- `/model` with only `--provider` keeps the current model name.
+- A switch that fails half way (a route dependent raises) is walked back by the binding; the test
+  checks the state after a failing fake binding.
+- `/approvals off` on a managed install → "managed" message; YAML `off` read back as False is
+  normalised by `approval_mode`.
+- `/queue` while idle with text → submitted now (nothing to wait for); while busy → queued and run by
+  `after_turn`.
+- `/steer` while idle → "nothing is running" (the reference falls back to a queue; we say so).
+
+Our design differences / decisions:
+- `/model --global` writes `model.default` + `model.provider`, and `base_url`/`api_mode` = "" when
+  the old saved provider was a custom endpoint and the new one differs.
+- `/reasoning` session change goes through `binding.apply(route, requested_effort=…)` (same
+  all-or-nothing path as `/model`).
+- `/usage` prints the session's token counters with cost `n/a` until P08.
+- Arrives with P17: the reference refuses some commands because its classic chat is a gateway
+  client; here they run in-process.
+
+Tests we will write:
+- `/model` while busy rejected; failing fake route rolls back; `--global` persists and clears a
+  stale custom base URL; `/approvals off` persists and is read back; managed install message;
+  `/yolo` stored on the row and restored for a resumed session; `/queue` runs after the turn;
+  `/help` grouping; `/tools disable` resets with a narrower selection; `/stop` kills jobs.
+
+## Decisions for the lead
+- `/steer` with no running turn prints a hint instead of queueing (simplest; easy to change).
+- `/tools enable|disable` take toolset names (`terminal`, `file`, `web`, …); a session selection
+  of "everything" is first expanded to the named sets the session actually has.
+
+Compare checklist (filled after the rewrite; reopened `hermes_cli/approval_mode.py`,
+`hermes_cli/cli_commands_mixin.py`):
+- [x] approvals: no arg shows, bad arg usage, managed/unreadable errors captured, read back
+  (tests: `test_control_cmds.py::test_approvals_*`)
+- [x] reasoning `--global` persists, else session only (test: `::test_reasoning_level_session_and_global`)
+- [x] `/stop` interrupts first, then stops background processes (test: `::test_stop_kills_jobs_and_interrupts`)
+- [x] `/queue` lists with no argument; `add` forces text that starts with a management word
+  (test: `::test_queue_management`)
+- Deliberate differences: `/model` has no picker or `--refresh` (P07 `indus model`); no `full`/`clamp`
+  reasoning display modes; `/reasoning show|hide` is per REPL session (the reference saves the
+  display choice to config); no `/queue edit|move` (P12).
+- Not taken: `/fast` (P08), `/busy`, `/footer`, `/timestamps`, `/statusbar` (TUI/P12 or later).
+
+## Status
+
+Done (2026-10-18).
